#Keep only the light part of the node json in memory, and read the heavy fields from disk only when asked. This is used to split the file in two, index.json which has each node's id, name, nodeType, dependencies, plus offset and length. payloads.ndjson is one line per node, contains columns and joinCondition. Once the file is split, do the lazy load. This means load just index.json, then measure and compare to step 2. Another function looks up a node's offset and length in the index, and jumps straight to that spot in the payload file (paylods.ndjson)